From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:20:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] media: intel/ipu6: Capture packed and 8-bit formats through
 the SoC raw pin

Formats stored at their own bit depth (8-bit, packed 10-bit) are captured
through the MIPI pin with long packet headers discarded. On the Microsoft
Surface Pro 9 most of those frames arrive truncated on both camera ports
("Transfer FIFO overflow", firmware error STR2MMIO): packed 10-bit from
the OV5693 109 of 110, from the VD55G0 197 of 211, 8-bit from the VD55G0
205 of 212. Through the SoC raw pin with the normal store mode, as the
unpacked formats already are, all of them arrive intact (0 errors), and
the unpacked formats, libcamera and PipeWire capture of all three cameras
are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-video.c | 17 ++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-video.c b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-video.c
index 3ac48d207..9fd484425 100644
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-video.c
@@ -481,9 +481,15 @@ static int ipu6_isys_fw_pin_cfg(struct ipu6_isys_video *av,
 	input_pin->mapped_dt = 0x40; /* invalid mipi data type */
 	input_pin->mipi_decompression = 0;
 	input_pin->capture_mode = IPU6_FW_ISYS_CAPTURE_MODE_REGULAR;
-	input_pin->mipi_store_mode = pfmt->bpp == pfmt->bpp_packed ?
-		IPU6_FW_ISYS_MIPI_STORE_MODE_DISCARD_LONG_HEADER :
-		IPU6_FW_ISYS_MIPI_STORE_MODE_NORMAL;
+	/*
+	 * The MIPI pin with long packet headers discarded, which upstream picks
+	 * for formats stored at their own bit depth (8-bit, packed 10-bit),
+	 * truncates most frames on the Surface Pro 9 (both camera ports,
+	 * "Transfer FIFO overflow", firmware error STR2MMIO). The SoC raw pin
+	 * with the normal store mode delivers them intact, as it does the
+	 * unpacked formats.
+	 */
+	input_pin->mipi_store_mode = IPU6_FW_ISYS_MIPI_STORE_MODE_NORMAL;
 	input_pin->crop_first_and_last_lines = v4l2_crop.top & 1;
 
 	output_pins = cfg->nof_output_pins++;
@@ -496,10 +502,7 @@ static int ipu6_isys_fw_pin_cfg(struct ipu6_isys_video *av,
 	output_pin->output_res.height = ipu6_isys_get_frame_height(av);
 
 	output_pin->stride = ipu6_isys_get_bytes_per_line(av);
-	if (pfmt->bpp != pfmt->bpp_packed)
-		output_pin->pt = IPU6_FW_ISYS_PIN_TYPE_RAW_SOC;
-	else
-		output_pin->pt = IPU6_FW_ISYS_PIN_TYPE_MIPI;
+	output_pin->pt = IPU6_FW_ISYS_PIN_TYPE_RAW_SOC;
 	output_pin->ft = pfmt->css_pixelformat;
 	output_pin->send_irq = 1;
 	memset(output_pin->ts_offsets, 0, sizeof(output_pin->ts_offsets));
